1
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:05,650
Hey, idiot. Wake up, already.

2
00:00:06,010 --> 00:00:06,900
It's so hot!

3
00:00:14,690 --> 00:00:16,250
<i>Time to switch to summer uniforms.</i>

4
00:00:37,470 --> 00:00:39,930
Can a Boy-Girl Friendship Survive?

5
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:39,930
(No, It Can't!!)

6
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:52,000
The Cracked Crocus

7
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:52,220
<i>I was so relieved about passing exams, 
I let work get away from me.</i>

8
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:55,480
<i>Now that Enomoto-san's joined the team,</i>

9
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:59,050
<i>I gotta work even harder as a creator.</i>

10
00:01:59,980 --> 00:02:04,310
<i>Like Saku-nee-san said, 
I need to quit being stuck in time.</i>

11
00:02:04,310 --> 00:02:06,060
Yu!

12
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:07,610
Morning!

13
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:11,770
M-Morning.

14
00:02:18,750 --> 00:02:20,370
<i>Well played, main model!</i>

15
00:02:20,370 --> 00:02:22,720
<i>You know my weakness!</i>

16
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:23,560
<i>But alas!</i>

17
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:25,580
Oh yeah, Himari.

18
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:28,990
You check out that dog post I sent you?

19
00:02:28,990 --> 00:02:30,160
Yup! Sure did!

20
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:32,900
I know you're just acting slick.

21
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:34,960
I see you eyeing my summer uniform!

22
00:02:35,510 --> 00:02:36,710
Shut up.

23
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:40,960
I'm still scarred over you humiliating me 
in front of the class last year.

24
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:42,860
Don't sweat it!

25
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:46,680
Everyone has a secret fetish or two.

26
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:49,960
I'm not shy about how much I love your eyes.

27
00:02:50,490 --> 00:02:52,600
You tell people that?

28
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:55,360
Won't that give people the wrong idea?

29
00:02:55,540 --> 00:02:57,360
Wrong idea how?

30
00:02:57,360 --> 00:03:01,200
<i>D-Dammit, she's trying to pressure me 
into saying it out loud.</i>

31
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:03,600
<i>But I'm a changed man!</i>

32
00:03:07,720 --> 00:03:09,750
You know exactly how.

33
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:13,220
People will look at us like we're dating.

34
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:19,560
Deep down, I bet you actually 
<i>want </i>to go out with me.

35
00:03:22,850 --> 00:03:26,880
<i>What's that look like she's
 so happy she can't contain herself?</i>

36
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:30,150
Then... what if we really went out?

37
00:03:33,070 --> 00:03:35,160
<i>What?! But we're in class—</i>

38
00:03:39,190 --> 00:03:41,280
<i>Wait. I know what happens next.</i>

39
00:03:43,870 --> 00:03:46,600
Ow! Come on, Yu!

40
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:50,240
Stop acting rebellious like Enocchi!

41
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:51,860
Shut up.

42
00:03:51,860 --> 00:03:54,690
It's not my fault you suck at romance!

43
00:03:54,690 --> 00:03:57,950
So much for trying to trick me.

44
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:01,320
<i>I wish I had a good comeback...</i>

45
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:06,210
So what's the plan today?

46
00:04:06,420 --> 00:04:09,890
Enomoto-san doesn't 
have band practice today,

47
00:04:10,970 --> 00:04:13,440
so I was thinking of having a team meeting.

48
00:04:13,970 --> 00:04:15,560
Yu-kun, Hii-chan.

49
00:04:18,020 --> 00:04:19,040
Sorry about the wait!

50
00:04:20,610 --> 00:04:22,960
Man, Enocchi. Those things are lethal.

51
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:24,950
You look nice in the summer uniform.

52
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:27,000
Th-Thanks.

53
00:04:30,890 --> 00:04:31,410
<i>Crap!</i>

54
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:34,300
<i>"That was nothing like 
your reaction to seeing me</i>

55
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:36,620
<i>glimmering under the bright 
summer sun. You prick!"</i>

56
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:37,920
<i>Is that it?</i>

57
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:41,470
U-Um, did you see my message?

58
00:04:41,890 --> 00:04:43,970
About the team meeting? Yup!

59
00:04:44,630 --> 00:04:46,090
Currently preparing to grow flowers!

60
00:04:46,380 --> 00:04:47,520
So what's the agenda?

61
00:04:47,790 --> 00:04:50,970
I think the first thing is what 
to do with our inventory.

62
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:54,980
Since preserved flowers 
change colors with time.

63
00:04:54,980 --> 00:04:56,390
Really?

64
00:04:56,390 --> 00:04:58,980
Then we should promote 
them as soon as we can.

65
00:04:59,230 --> 00:05:03,560
Yup! So next, we shoot promos 
and post them online. Right?

66
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:10,910
R-Right, with Himari as the model.

67
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:16,490
Gee, I hope that didn't seem
 like a leading question!

68
00:05:16,830 --> 00:05:19,460
Whatever it was, I don't like it.

69
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:21,550
Oh, there he is!

70
00:05:21,550 --> 00:05:22,710
Natsume-kun!

71
00:05:23,050 --> 00:05:26,480
Hey Himari-san! And Enomoto-san!

72
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:31,090
Woah, this is a crazy good-looking group.

73
00:05:31,090 --> 00:05:35,310
Hey, Mao-py and Azu-kyun! What's up?

74
00:05:35,450 --> 00:05:39,770
We wanted to ask about those accessories 
you promised us the other day!

75
00:05:41,970 --> 00:05:42,880
Oh yeah!

76
00:05:43,650 --> 00:05:45,400
Science Room

77
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:46,780
Phew.

78
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:50,440
You can take any of the ones in here.

79
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:53,310
No, that's not special enough!

80
00:05:53,310 --> 00:05:55,360
We want custom ones!

81
00:05:56,260 --> 00:05:57,870
I figured you might say that.

82
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:03,280
Could you start by letting 
us know what you want?

83
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:06,050
Custom-made pieces can get expensive.

84
00:06:06,050 --> 00:06:07,880
So you might wanna think about your budget.

85
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:10,360
And besides...

86
00:06:11,220 --> 00:06:12,950
Yu decides what pieces to make.

87
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:18,740
My bad. I thought it was 
the same as the other ones.

88
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:22,760
See, it's Mao and her boyfriend's 
anniversary next month.

89
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:25,540
I wanted a matching pair of accessories,

90
00:06:25,540 --> 00:06:27,820
but haven't been able to find any that work.

91
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:32,770
You mean you want a piece for a guy 
and girl under the same concept?

92
00:06:32,770 --> 00:06:33,740
Exactly!

93
00:06:34,340 --> 00:06:35,300
<i>Not a bad idea.</i>

94
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:38,480
<i>A matching set would be a new challenge.</i>

95
00:06:40,700 --> 00:06:42,960
Looks like Yu's up for it!

96
00:06:44,250 --> 00:06:45,500
Yay!

97
00:06:48,490 --> 00:06:50,090
That was exhausting.

98
00:06:50,340 --> 00:06:53,000
Yu, you gotta toughen up.

99
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:57,960
Creators have to engage 
with customers in this day and age!

100
00:06:57,960 --> 00:07:00,850
Yeah, but those two are so outgoing.

101
00:07:00,850 --> 00:07:02,990
I want customers who are a bit tamer.

102
00:07:03,440 --> 00:07:04,680
Keeping notes...

103
00:07:05,010 --> 00:07:08,970
"That face means Yu-kun's up for it."

104
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:10,160
Is that necessary?

105
00:07:10,710 --> 00:07:13,810
So we're going to plan 
something for those two,

106
00:07:13,810 --> 00:07:16,720
while clearing out inventory. Sound good?

107
00:07:17,590 --> 00:07:18,450
Okay!

108
00:07:19,830 --> 00:07:20,850
Roger that.

109
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:26,880
About the flower for this piece...

110
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:29,120
I'm thinking the Japanese cornel.

111
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:30,940
Cornel?

112
00:07:31,090 --> 00:07:34,350
Umm... This?

113
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:39,050
It represents maintenance, 
resilience, and mature spirit.

114
00:07:39,050 --> 00:07:43,000
But why this? Kinda has 
an old lady vibe, doesn't it?

115
00:07:43,410 --> 00:07:46,820
Remember when we met with that couple?

116
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:54,770
Instead of an intense love, 
they gave off a tangible vibe.

117
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:58,830
The Japanese cornel is the flower of health.

118
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:02,190
If we're talking about a long, 
sustainable relationship,

119
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:05,270
I thought something more 
down-to-earth would suit them.

120
00:08:06,260 --> 00:08:08,670
You think it's a bit too cheesy?

121
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:10,760
Don't say that.

122
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,590
It's ultimately up to the customer,

123
00:08:12,590 --> 00:08:16,280
but we respect your vision as the creator.

124
00:08:16,530 --> 00:08:17,190
Yup!

125
00:08:17,630 --> 00:08:19,050
Th-Thanks.

126
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:21,600
What about the price?

127
00:08:21,820 --> 00:08:23,330
That's the only hang-up...

128
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:25,680
Is there a problem?

129
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:30,350
Honestly, I think our prices right now 
are too expensive for high schoolers.

130
00:08:30,580 --> 00:08:35,610
Yeah, teenagers only make up 
10% of our customers overall.

131
00:08:35,970 --> 00:08:38,340
And we've flown under 
the radar at school so far

132
00:08:38,980 --> 00:08:41,910
since everything has been
sold through social media.

133
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:44,590
But there's other girls like me...

134
00:08:44,790 --> 00:08:47,240
Yeah, and now that people know who you are,

135
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:50,040
you might be getting a lot more attention.

136
00:08:50,580 --> 00:08:52,680
Is it bad if I get more attention?

137
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:53,930
Well what if girls—

138
00:08:53,390 --> 00:08:56,000
You might get really popular with girls!

139
00:08:56,840 --> 00:09:00,290
Enomoto-san, don't say dumb stuff like that.

140
00:09:00,290 --> 00:09:01,650
D-Dumb...?

141
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:04,640
Sorry! It slipped out!

142
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:06,520
I reacted like I would with Himari!

143
00:09:07,590 --> 00:09:10,740
That means I'm catching up 
to Hii-chan, right?

144
00:09:10,740 --> 00:09:12,150
You're so positive...

145
00:09:12,550 --> 00:09:15,980
I guess it's not a bad thing 
for customers to come to you.

146
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:16,870
Yeah.

147
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:22,440
I'll try to engage with 
customers more for You's sake.

148
00:09:24,150 --> 00:09:28,750
<i>It might just be the breakthrough I need, 
like Saku-nee-san said.</i>

149
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:33,420
A Few Days Later

150
00:09:31,870 --> 00:09:33,420
Wow!

151
00:09:33,420 --> 00:09:36,270
I've never heard of the Japanese cornel.

152
00:09:36,270 --> 00:09:38,240
But it's so pretty! Isn't it?

153
00:09:38,410 --> 00:09:39,340
Yeah.

154
00:09:39,730 --> 00:09:41,160
It'll look nice on you, Mao.

155
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:42,560
You think so?

156
00:09:42,890 --> 00:09:43,870
Pardon me.

157
00:09:45,350 --> 00:09:47,520
I'm not very good with accessories...

158
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:51,410
Senpai, you have a good frame 
so I think it'll suit you.

159
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:55,910
Necklaces shouldn't be tucked away, 
they need to be shown off.

160
00:09:56,160 --> 00:09:57,340
Makes sense.

161
00:09:57,730 --> 00:10:03,020
You know, I was a bit shy 
about the matching set thing,

162
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:08,920
but she really liked the piece 
she bought from you last year.

163
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:12,330
And you were so open to our thoughts, too.

164
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:29,440
<i>Like I thought, when 
people love each other...</i>

165
00:10:31,330 --> 00:10:33,150
<i>It's just so beautiful in my eyes.</i>

166
00:10:37,290 --> 00:10:42,160
Um, I heard that you could order 
custom-made accessories here?

167
00:10:43,290 --> 00:10:44,900
There's a rumor going around

168
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:48,980
that you can make something perfect 
to fit people and their crush.

169
00:10:50,930 --> 00:10:53,340
She's the fifth person just today.

170
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:54,760
That's so many.

171
00:10:55,110 --> 00:10:57,680
Looks like Mao-py and Azu-kyun 
have been spreading the word.

172
00:10:58,650 --> 00:11:00,640
Word-of-mouth beats any ad.

173
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:02,740
The matching set was great,

174
00:11:02,740 --> 00:11:06,350
but that earring you made Azu-kyun 
was really cute, too.

175
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:09,560
People have been asking me 
about it in band, too.

176
00:11:09,560 --> 00:11:10,470
For real?

177
00:11:10,830 --> 00:11:12,980
We gotta find the time to make them.

178
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:15,320
Science Room

179
00:11:16,490 --> 00:11:17,240
Wow.

180
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:20,520
You wanted a feminine, 
Japanese design, right?

181
00:11:21,740 --> 00:11:23,540
Thanks.

182
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:27,240
This means he'll fall for me, 
like the rumors said!

183
00:11:29,570 --> 00:11:30,840
Hi there!

184
00:11:31,340 --> 00:11:35,510
Is it true that You's accessories will 
make your crush fall in love with you?

185
00:11:37,350 --> 00:11:41,550
People are getting carried away 
with this made-to-order thing.

186
00:11:41,550 --> 00:11:45,030
They're more willing to pay 
the hiked price since

187
00:11:45,030 --> 00:11:49,810
these are completely unique pieces, 
unlike the ones before.

188
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:53,170
And those two are too good 
at promoting this stuff!

189
00:11:53,780 --> 00:11:55,610
Don't be shy!

190
00:11:55,610 --> 00:11:59,080
We can totally spread 
the word on how great these are!

191
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:00,910
Leave it to us!

192
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:03,570
It started as an "original" accessory.

193
00:12:03,570 --> 00:12:06,160
Then it became a "one-of-a-kind 
accessory made to order."

194
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:09,730
Now it's an accessory that'll "make 
your romantic wishes come true."

195
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:11,800
Can't we ask them to hold off on promo?

196
00:12:12,220 --> 00:12:14,480
How can we? They're so happy to do it.

197
00:12:15,650 --> 00:12:18,590
You have to admit, it <i>is</i> nice of them.

198
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:20,410
We'll just have to power through it.

199
00:12:22,610 --> 00:12:24,470
Yu! How's it going?

200
00:12:24,650 --> 00:12:28,010
I'm amazed at this space 
Hibari-san prepared for me.

201
00:12:29,430 --> 00:12:33,100
Oh, and sorry to be here while you're out.

202
00:12:33,390 --> 00:12:34,620
It's fine.

203
00:12:34,620 --> 00:12:39,950
We can't leave the science room 
unattended in case a new client pops in.

204
00:12:39,950 --> 00:12:40,690
I appreciate it.

205
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:44,040
I can hardly get anything done 
at home thanks to Daifuku.

206
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:47,540
So I might be cooped up in here for a while.

207
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:49,440
Shouldn't you get some rest?

208
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:51,020
I'll wake you up when Enocchi gets here.

209
00:12:52,230 --> 00:12:52,960
What are you doing?

210
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:56,410
Inviting you to rest on my 
cute little lap, of course.

211
00:12:56,660 --> 00:12:58,920
You can't be stupid enough 
to decline this offer.

212
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:02,570
<i>You being cute is exactly 
why I'd have to decline.</i>

213
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:07,190
<i>Oh well. It's not like anyone will see.</i>

214
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:12,400
"If this were Enocchi, I bet 
I wouldn't be able to see her face."

215
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:14,020
Is that what you're thinking?

216
00:13:14,020 --> 00:13:15,900
O-Of course not!

217
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:18,480
Himari-san, napping on your lap is the best!

218
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:22,280
Ew, are you picking up phrases 
from Makishima-kun?

219
00:13:22,590 --> 00:13:27,890
Don't even think about copying that player.

220
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:29,940
Cut the crap. Let me sleep.

221
00:13:32,090 --> 00:13:33,900
Himari. Can I ask you something?

222
00:13:35,230 --> 00:13:38,460
Remember when I made 
a piece for Enomoto-san?

223
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:41,700
You said you wanted an accessory of romance.

224
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:43,680
Oh my gosh, that's so embarrassing.

225
00:13:46,190 --> 00:13:48,640
Why do you ask? You 
feeling romance towards me?

226
00:13:48,940 --> 00:13:52,080
Shut up. But what about you?

227
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:56,560
You had a bad experience 
with Makishima's exes in middle school.

228
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:58,930
You've hated romance ever since? Even now?

229
00:13:59,450 --> 00:14:00,960
Hmm...

230
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:03,240
Yup!

231
00:14:03,870 --> 00:14:06,600
Then why did you ask 
for a piece about romance?

232
00:14:07,650 --> 00:14:11,490
Because Enocchi looked so cute in hers.

233
00:14:11,750 --> 00:14:13,240
Oh... Okay.

234
00:14:14,730 --> 00:14:17,920
<i>I was afraid it meant she fell 
for another guy.</i>

235
00:14:19,050 --> 00:14:22,690
<i>I always thought I'd be fine 
if Himari got a boyfriend.</i>

236
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:26,990
<i>But now... even if 
it's just as a best friend,</i>

237
00:14:26,990 --> 00:14:28,440
<i>I want her by my side forever.</i>

238
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:33,570
<i>Himari's nice enough 
to do that if I ask her.</i>

239
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:39,470
<i>But I don't wanna take 
advantage of her like that.</i>

240
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:46,400
<i>That's why I need to work 
harder... to be her equal...</i>

241
00:14:59,530 --> 00:15:02,380
<i>I wonder if it's because 
he's been so focused on work.</i>

242
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:04,640
<i>Yu's clearly changed.</i>

243
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:09,050
<i>Before, all he needed 
was to satisfy himself.</i>

244
00:15:10,060 --> 00:15:12,560
<i>But now, his eyes are burning with passion.</i>

245
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:15,360
<i>He gives me goosebumps now.</i>

246
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:18,150
<i>And it scares me at the same time.</i>

247
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:21,980
<i>Like he might leave me 
and go off on his own.</i>

248
00:15:23,050 --> 00:15:24,620
<i>I hate romance.</i>

249
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:28,260
<i>Thanks to all these girls caught up in love,</i>

250
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:30,560
<i>I've had less time with Yu recently.</i>

251
00:15:30,770 --> 00:15:31,960
<i>What a drag.</i>

252
00:15:32,810 --> 00:15:34,620
<i>I don't need a piece about romance.</i>

253
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:38,860
<i>As long as I have this best friend ring,</i>

254
00:15:39,150 --> 00:15:41,640
<i>Yu will stay by my side.</i>

255
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:47,470
<i>But if anyone were to ask 
if I wanted to go back</i>

256
00:15:47,470 --> 00:15:50,400
<i>to the days when we were only friends...</i>

257
00:15:51,240 --> 00:15:53,210
<i>My answer would be "no."</i>

258
00:15:54,580 --> 00:15:57,230
<i>Because if I never realized that I loved Yu,</i>

259
00:15:57,420 --> 00:16:00,580
<i>I wouldn't have known 
the happiness I do now.</i>

260
00:16:03,350 --> 00:16:07,560
<i>I'm probably living the happiest 
days of my life right now.</i>

261
00:16:08,410 --> 00:16:11,350
<i>I'm not exaggerating. It's true.</i>

262
00:16:14,940 --> 00:16:19,040
So we're delivering two pieces today.

263
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:21,560
Let's break up into groups 
so we can deliver these—

264
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:27,640
I thought I saw a guy 
with some gorgeous girls.

265
00:16:27,640 --> 00:16:29,720
And what do you know? It's Natsu!

266
00:16:31,970 --> 00:16:34,050
Hey, Makishima-kun. Can we help you?

267
00:16:34,050 --> 00:16:36,100
You don't have to copy her, Enomoto-san.

268
00:16:36,650 --> 00:16:37,890
Remember, Rin-chan.

269
00:16:37,890 --> 00:16:40,940
Too much physical contact 
makes it less special.

270
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:43,900
Save that for the right moment 
to leave an impression.

271
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:45,960
Oh! Right!

272
00:16:46,510 --> 00:16:48,990
Don't make note of that.

273
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:53,240
Rin-chan sure makes a great student.

274
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:57,200
She'll beat out Himari-chan 
in no time, don't you worry.

275
00:16:57,570 --> 00:16:59,060
You know, Makishima-kun.

276
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:01,000
Instead of focusing 
on other people's love lives,

277
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:04,200
you should make sure your younger 
girlfriend doesn't get fed up of you.

278
00:17:04,770 --> 00:17:06,140
More importantly, Natsu.

279
00:17:06,140 --> 00:17:08,540
Wanna grab a bite to eat?

280
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:11,280
I thought we could discuss 
the future of You.

281
00:17:13,530 --> 00:17:16,840
Did you put those two up 
to promoting my accessories?

282
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:19,820
Nope, that was entirely their choice.

283
00:17:20,420 --> 00:17:23,550
They may be part of the popular crowd,

284
00:17:23,550 --> 00:17:26,040
but they're friendly 
with any circle of students.

285
00:17:26,380 --> 00:17:30,440
They love being in other people's business 
but act purely on good intentions.

286
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:31,750
Yeah?

287
00:17:32,210 --> 00:17:36,470
That's why they were the perfect pair 
to help leak the creator of You.

288
00:17:37,550 --> 00:17:38,530
What do you mean?

289
00:17:38,890 --> 00:17:45,160
Even 100% good intentions can
sometimes turn into 200% ill intentions.

290
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:47,140
I have no clue what you're talking about.

291
00:17:47,140 --> 00:17:50,410
I wanted to talk to you 
to apologize beforehand.

292
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:52,980
If everything goes as expected,

293
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:55,600
you might be in for some emotional pain.

294
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:58,780
What? Why would you do that?

295
00:17:58,780 --> 00:18:00,640
For Rin-chan, of course.

296
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:03,190
I'm totally lost.

297
00:18:03,190 --> 00:18:05,860
Why are you so invested 
in helping Enomoto-san anyways?

298
00:18:06,790 --> 00:18:08,830
Because I owe Rin-chan.

299
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:14,280
Something worth way more than 
helping her realize her first love.

300
00:18:17,690 --> 00:18:24,290
<i>It wasn't long before I found out 
the full scope of Makishima's plans.</i>

301
00:18:25,430 --> 00:18:27,700
Did you make this?

302
00:18:28,190 --> 00:18:29,410
Y-Yes...

303
00:18:31,120 --> 00:18:36,740
We received a complaint from the parents 
of the female student who bought this.

304
00:18:36,950 --> 00:18:38,210
A complaint?

305
00:18:38,810 --> 00:18:43,720
They say their daughter was coerced 
into buying this accessory for a high price.

306
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:45,500
That's not what happened at all!

307
00:18:45,770 --> 00:18:49,910
We made this based on her requests 
and shared the price in advance.

308
00:18:50,230 --> 00:18:51,570
She agreed to it.

309
00:18:52,060 --> 00:18:53,780
Is there proof of that?

310
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:59,830
Only a statement of delivery and receipt...

311
00:19:00,130 --> 00:19:01,280
But that's with Himari.

312
00:19:01,530 --> 00:19:04,240
Okay then. I'll ask Inuzuka about that.

313
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:10,250
By the way, are your handmade 
accessories sold according to regulations?

314
00:19:10,690 --> 00:19:15,950
O-Our accessories are accounted under 
my family's convenience store business.

315
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:19,660
We've undergone legal processes,
and my sister manages that side.

316
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:23,460
That's right, your sister's Sakura.

317
00:19:23,840 --> 00:19:26,250
You've been a handful with your blank exams.

318
00:19:26,250 --> 00:19:29,030
But Sakura was a handful for being so smart.

319
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:33,670
I'll have to discuss 
with the other teachers first,

320
00:19:33,950 --> 00:19:37,290
but even if the school determines 
your activities are no issue,

321
00:19:37,690 --> 00:19:40,590
the same can't be said 
for other parents who don't know you.

322
00:19:41,270 --> 00:19:46,700
All they know is that their kid bought 
an expensive accessory.

323
00:19:47,210 --> 00:19:48,000
Understand?

324
00:19:48,650 --> 00:19:49,420
Yes, sir.

325
00:19:49,630 --> 00:19:51,720
I won't tell you to stop making them.

326
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:53,910
But you'll have to pause sales 
for the time being.

327
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:58,010
Any orders you've already 
accepted will have to wait. Okay?

328
00:19:59,290 --> 00:20:01,550
What? That's ridiculous!

329
00:20:01,870 --> 00:20:04,380
She sounds like a Karen in the making!

330
00:20:04,780 --> 00:20:08,500
Thankfully, Sasaki-sensei 
did some damage control.

331
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:11,230
We're lucky to get off this easy.

332
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:14,230
But we'll have to assert ourselves more.

333
00:20:14,230 --> 00:20:16,300
She's the one lying, after all.

334
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:19,900
Man, that was such a waste of money.

335
00:20:20,390 --> 00:20:22,920
We only did it cause Senpai told us to.

336
00:20:23,130 --> 00:20:24,400
Exactly!

337
00:20:24,400 --> 00:20:25,890
So dumb!

338
00:20:27,510 --> 00:20:29,760
I only bought that expensive thing because

339
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:32,170
they promised it would 
make him like me back!

340
00:20:32,170 --> 00:20:34,080
You think we can return it?

341
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:38,160
So I can admit to them I got dumped? No way.

342
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:40,880
I bet it's all to make more money.

343
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:43,480
I hate Senpai for dumping me.

344
00:20:43,770 --> 00:20:45,550
And whoever spread that rumor.

345
00:20:45,910 --> 00:20:48,090
And that guy who made this!

346
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:50,400
They can all go to hell!

347
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:54,240
<i>She said she had a crush 
on another senpai from her club.</i>

348
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:59,440
<i>She wanted a feminine, 
Japanese-style piece he would like.</i>

349
00:21:00,450 --> 00:21:02,360
<i>Seeing her talk about her love for him...</i>

350
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:06,280
<i>I thought it was beautiful 
how innocent and giddy she looked.</i>

351
00:21:07,590 --> 00:21:08,730
Hey!

352
00:21:08,730 --> 00:21:11,560
A lot of work went into that!

353
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:13,700
Why would you do something like that?!

354
00:21:13,700 --> 00:21:14,870
Let me go!

355
00:21:14,870 --> 00:21:16,340
It's not worth it! Let's go!

356
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:22,650
<i>Having feelings for someone 
is a beautiful thing.</i>

357
00:21:23,880 --> 00:21:26,280
<i>Like how I realized my feelings for Himari,</i>

358
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:28,980
<i>and how that motivated me 
to be a better person.</i>

359
00:21:40,890 --> 00:21:44,080
But "beautiful" doesn't always mean "pure."

360
00:21:45,080 --> 00:21:46,040
Yu-kun...

361
00:21:47,750 --> 00:21:48,850
<i>She was right.</i>

362
00:21:49,660 --> 00:21:51,960
<i>Even something 
as beautiful as loving someone</i>

363
00:21:53,250 --> 00:21:56,050
<i>doesn't necessarily mean 
their intentions are pure.</i>

364
00:21:57,710 --> 00:21:59,190
<i>Realizing that made me feel...</i>

365
00:21:59,190 --> 00:22:04,200
<i>like a huge piece of shit.</i>

366
00:23:35,220 --> 00:23:39,930
Zinnia and Where Passion Lies

